`git-annex push -C.` to an exporttree=yes remote sends the whole tree, not
only files in the specified directory.

That behavior is documented, but seems suboptimal. It should be possible to
limit what is exported to the specified directory, and notice if there were
any files outside that in the tree that are not present on the remote. If
there are none, the tree export can be recorded as complete. If there are
other files, leave the tree export incomplete. --[[Joey]]
